messages:
maya (Docs): Pushing a tiny docs PR to clarify SOC2/audit log wording + add a node SDK header example and a retention API sample. Need quick legal+security scan before merge.

trent (Security): Sounds good. Quick asks: 1) use 'recommended' not a hard promise for retention numbers; 2) call out append-only storage + integrity monitoring; 3) mention PII redaction options.

sara (Legal): Agreed. Also add that retention can be extended for legal/regulatory reasons and that customer contracts may set the retention. Don't publish firm guarantees unless in SLA.

maya (Docs): Draft snippet I'll add:
```js
// attach audit metadata for traceability
await client.generate({
  model: 'rw-instruct-1',
  input: 'Summarize this',
  headers: { 'x-redwood-audit-id': 'acct-42-evt-1001' }
});
```

lee (DevEx): small nit: use "Redwood retains" instead of "we retain". Also include an example retention API payload for Dedicated customers.

maya (Docs): Retention example I'll add:
```json
{
  "policy_name": "prod-default",
  "retention_days": 730,
  "redaction": { "pii_fields": ["email"], "method": "mask" }
}
```

trent (Security): Add one liner: "Audit logs are stored append-only with integrity checks; deletions are logged and require authorization." Good for auditors.

sara (Legal): +1. Also note: "Recommended retention: 90 days (dev), 24 months (prod). Actual retention is configurable and subject to customer agreements and law." That phrasing keeps us safe.

maya (Docs): Thanks all. One last link check: redaction guide anchor is /docs/data-redaction#audit-logs ? If that's wrong I'll update after infra confirms.

infra-bot: docs build queued: CI: ✅, staging: ✅

maya (Docs): Perfect. I'll update the PR with these edits and merge after legal sign-off. Thanks! :raised_hands:
